{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfwy9G8eur3a2ThuCT9Mo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In Vitest 5.x, `testNamePattern` (the `-t` flag) matches against the test's full name. The full name is the enclosing suite names plus the test name, joined with **`\" > \"`** (space, greater-than, space). It's the same string the reporter prints, for example `math > add > handles negatives`. Because the pattern sees the whole path, you can target a test nested in a suite with something like `-t \"add > handles\"`.\n\nI got this from the project's Ludion lessons file (`.ludion/lessons.md`), which says the matching changed in Vitest 5.0.0 (installed: 5.0.3). I couldn't check it against Vitest's own code because `node_modules` doesn't have the Vitest packages installed here. If you depend on the exact behaviour, check the Vitest 5 changelog."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":388,"cache_read_input_tokens":28167,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":388},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c52206df-eab8-4580-938d-25f2a755a2f6","uuid":"b2e99c00-9894-4a38-816e-5f2d4c0868ef","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:43:49.367Z","request_id":"req_011Cfwy9Fp43cDGu1KPZL2W3"}
